<title>ABU DHABI: Arab fund approves economic reform aid.</title>
<headline>Arab fund approves economic reform aid.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Arab Monetary Fund (AMF) said on Sunday it had approved a $540 million programme to support economic reforms in Arab states.</p>
<p>The support will involve loans to member states for financial and monetary reforms, said an AMF statement released at the annual meeting of Arab finance ministers and central bank governors.</p>
<p>The Abu Dhabi-based AMF -- the Arab world's premier financial institution -- was set up by 20 Arab governments in 1977 to lay the foundations for Arab economic integration and promote economic development.</p>
<p>It provides soft loans to assist in financing balance of payments deficits in support of economic adjustment programmes.</p>
</text>
